.TH SHITFETCH 1 "2026-05-26" "shitfetch 0.1.0" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
shitfetch \- minimal Linux fetch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shitfetch
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shitfetch
prints a compact system summary with an ASCII logo, hardware and session data,
and a package count assembled from supported system package databases.
.PP
The program is Linux-only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-logo " NAME"
Select a logo by name. Use
.B none
to disable logo output.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo= NAME
Equivalent to
.BR "\-l NAME" .
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-template " TEMPLATE"
Select the output template. Supported values are
.B default
and
.BR mini .
.TP
.BI \-\-template= TEMPLATE
Equivalent to
.BR "\-t TEMPLATE" .
.TP
.BI \-\-modules " CSV"
Set module order from a comma-separated list. Example:
.BR os,kernel,shell,local-ip .
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " PATH"
Load configuration from
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-config= PATH
Equivalent to
.BR "\-c PATH" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Disable automatic configuration lookup.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin [= AXIS ]
Animate the logo as a spinning 2.5D relief before printing the static output.
.I AXIS
is
.BR x ,
.BR y ,
or
.B xy
(default). The animation needs a terminal on both standard input and standard
output; otherwise it is skipped silently.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-speed " N"
Rotation rate in radians per second, 0.05 to 20. Default 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-size " N"
Projection scale, 0.5 to 5. Default 1, which maps one source cell onto one
terminal cell. Larger values grow the relief until it runs out of terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-depth " N"
Relief thickness, 0.1 to 10. The default 0 derives the thickness from the
variance of the logo's glyph density, so flat single-glyph art still gets a
solid body.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-height " N"
Relief height in rows, 6 to 200. The default 0 takes the taller of the info
panel and the logo's own height, capped by the terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-frames " N"
Stop after
.I N
frames. The default 0 runs until a key is pressed.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-fps " N"
Target frame rate, 1 to 120. Default 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-light " DIR"
Light direction:
.BR top\-left " (default), " top ", " top\-right ", " left ", " front ", " right ", "
.BR bottom\-left ", " bottom ", or " bottom\-right .
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-shade " MODE"
Glyph alphabet the relief is drawn with:
.BR auto " (default), " ascii ", " braille ", or " blocks .
.B ascii
writes one character of the shading ramp per cell.
.B braille
and
.B blocks
rasterize a 2x4 and a 2x2 subpixel grid inside each cell instead. A cell the
relief only partly covers becomes the glyph for exactly those subpixels, so an
edge lands on a fraction of a cell rather than snapping to the character grid; a
fully covered cell carries brightness instead, as one of the four shade blocks
in
.B blocks
mode and as dot density in
.BR braille .
.B auto
reads what the logo art itself is made of: braille art gets
.BR braille ,
block\-element art gets
.BR blocks ,
and everything else gets
.BR ascii .
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-chars " STR"
Shading ramp from darkest to brightest, used by the
.B ascii
shading mode. Default
.BR .,\-~:;=!*#$@ .
.SH SPIN
.B \-\-spin
extrudes the logo along Z by the visual ink weight of each glyph, rotates the
resulting point cloud, and shades it per frame; nothing is pre-rendered. The
info panel stays in its usual place on the right, with
.BR uptime ,
.BR memory ,
and
.B swap
refreshed once per second. The relief is given only as many columns as the
rotating logo needs, so the panel sits where the static layout puts it, and the
.B colors
swatches follow the panel just as they do in static output.
.PP
The animation is drawn in place, in the same rows a normal run would occupy, so
nothing above it is cleared and the scrollback is left intact. Those rows are
erased and the cursor and terminal mode are restored on a keypress,
.BR SIGINT ,
.BR SIGTERM ,
or
.BR SIGHUP .
The static output is printed afterwards either way, which makes
.B \-\-spin
usable as a shell startup fetch. A logo of
.B none
disables it.
.SH CONFIGURATION
If automatic configuration loading is enabled,
.B shitfetch
looks for:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/shitfetch/config.jsonc\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fB$HOME/.config/shitfetch/config.jsonc\fR when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set
.PP
See
.BR shitfetch (5)
for the configuration format.
.SH TEMPLATES
.TP
.B default
Shows the full default module set and ANSI color block.
.TP
.B mini
Uses compact logos and a reduced module set:
.BR os ,
.BR kernel ,
.BR init ,
.BR wm/de ,
.BR pkgs ,
.BR shell ,
and
.BR memory .
.SH MODULES
Built-in modules are:
.BR os ,
.BR kernel ,
.BR init ,
.BR uptime ,
.BR host ,
.BR shell ,
.BR wm ,
.BR term ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR gpu ,
.BR memory ,
.BR swap ,
.BR disk ,
.BR packages ,
.BR display ,
.BR locale ,
and
.BR local-ip .
.PP
Aliases include
.BR dewm ,
.BR wm/de ,
.BR terminal ,
.BR pkgs ,
.BR lang ,
.BR local_ip ,
and
.BR ip .
.SH PACKAGE DETECTION
The
.B packages
module currently supports these system package managers:
.BR pacman ,
.BR dpkg ,
.BR apk ,
.BR xbps ,
.BR pkgtools ,
.BR scratchpkg ,
.BR paludis ,
.BR portage ,
.BR sorcery ,
.BR kiss ,
.BR cpt ,
.BR butch ,
.BR tazpkg ,
.BR pisi ,
.BR pkgsrc ,
.BR cards ,
.BR pkgutils ,
.BR gobo ,
.BR opkg ,
.BR eopkg ,
.BR swupd ,
.BR nix ,
.BR guix ,
.BR flatpak ,
.BR snap ,
.BR macports ,
and
.BR homebrew .
.PP
Counts are taken from local package database state only; language-specific
package managers are intentionally ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/shitfetch/config.jsonc
Default per-user configuration file when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/shitfetch/config.jsonc
Preferred per-user configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, invalid configuration, or runtime failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shitfetch (5),
.BR shitfetch (7)
